  "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x-7 & =0.5 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061x & =7.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(7.5)=1.438\\,244\u2026\u22481.4\n$$\n\nSince $1.4$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=1.4.$\n\nTo generate solutions in the domain, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +1.438\\,244\u2026\u22484.6.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order and rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are $x=1.4$ and $x=4.6.$",
